7. Extensions

The following two extensions are stated in conceptual form. They are not developed to the standard of the core analysis and are not claimed as results.

7.1 Multiplanetary latency

Earth–Mars one-way light-time ranges from approximately 3 to 22 minutes depending on orbital geometry; round-trip latency ranges 6 to 44 minutes. The local-autonomy threshold becomes time-dependent:

\tau_{\text{local},i} + 2 L(t) \ge \tau_c(h^*_i) \quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad L(t) \ge \frac{\tau_c(h^*_i) - \tau_{\text{local},i}}{2}, \tag{7.1}

where \tau_c(h^*_i) is given by (4.5). The viability-required autonomy window is the fraction of a synodic period during which (7.1) holds:

W_i = \frac{1}{T_{\text{synodic}}} \int_0^{T_{\text{synodic}}} \mathbf{1}\!\left[L(t) \ge \frac{\tau_c(h^*_i) - \tau_{\text{local},i}}{2}\right] dt. \tag{7.2}

Information quality available to a central coordinator decays with latency as q_{\text{central}}(L) = q_0 e^{-\alpha L} with \alpha \ge 0. The local autonomy condition becomes

q_{\text{local}} > q_0 \exp\!\big(-(\alpha + 2\lambda_i) L(t)\big). \tag{7.3}

This is testable in principle: \alpha can be estimated from empirical studies of distributed decision quality versus latency, and q_{\text{local}} from polycentric-governance case data. No such estimation is performed here.

7.2 Fat-tailed hazards

For heavy-tailed hazard processes, the log-amplification \mathcal{M} = \lambda \tau is not the operative risk indicator. A jump-diffusion extension is

dh(t) = \lambda h(t)\, dt - a_{\text{eff}} h(t) g(h(t-\tau))\, dt + \sigma h(t)\, dW(t) + h(t^-) \int_{\mathbb{R}} (e^z - 1) \widetilde N(dt, dz), \tag{7.4}

where \widetilde N is a compensated Poisson measure. The risk indicator is the expected shortfall of the reserve path, computed by peaks-over-threshold fitting of reserve-deficit exceedances to a generalized Pareto distribution with shape \xi and scale \beta. When \xi \ge 1, expected shortfall is infinite and the system is in a precautionary regime.

The stochastic delay equation (7.4) requires existence and uniqueness conditions that are not stated here; the extension is therefore conceptual. A rigorous treatment would require globally Lipschitz coefficients and bounded jumps, or an explicit citation to a well-posedness theorem, and the reserve process would need to be shown to be a well-defined semimartingale before peaks-over-threshold fitting is meaningful.

